782 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/Alt (Twelve memory dies fanned over their base die\054 drawn face up\056 In a real stack each faces down\056 TSVs\054 copper\055filled holes\054 carry signals through the stack\054 and microbumps join each die to the next\056 A drawn notch shows both\056 The footprint is 11 by 11 mm\054 as Micron gives for its twelve\055high HBM3E\056 The dies are drawn far thicker and farther apart than they are\056 Before HBM4\054 a finished stack could be at most 720 micrometers tall\054 an SK hynix newsroom tech note says\056)
